---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LineChart from "../components/LineChart.astro";
import PeriodTable from "../components/PeriodTable.astro";
import StackedBars from "../components/StackedBars.astro";
import fs from "node:fs";
import { series, latest } from "../lib/data.js";
import { num, period } from "../lib/format.js";

const g = series("gdp_real_growth");
const last = latest(g);
const nominal = series("gdp_nominal_level");
const sectors = ["agri", "mining", "mfg", "utilities", "construction", "trade", "finance", "public"];
const components = ["pfce", "gfce", "gfcf", "exports", "imports"];
const lastLevel = latest(nominal);
const contrib = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync("src/data/generated/gdp_contributions.json", "utf8"));
const other = contrib.rows.filter((r) => r.component.startsWith("Other")).at(-1);
---
<Base current="growth" title="Growth">
  <h1>Growth</h1>
  <p class="lede">How fast is the economy growing, and which sectors and spending components drive it? Quarterly national accounts from MoSPI. Real GDP grew {num(last.value, 1)}% on a year earlier in {period(last.period, "Q")}; nominal GDP in that quarter was ₹{num(lastLevel.value, 1)} lakh crore.</p>

  <LineChart title="Real GDP and GVA growth, as published" subtitle="% change on the same quarter a year earlier, constant prices"
    lines={[{ id: "gdp_real_growth", label: "GDP" }, { id: "gva_real_growth", label: "GVA" }]} years={10} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Base 2022-23 from Q1 FY24 (April–June 2023), base 2011-12 before; each value is the rate MoSPI published on that base. The swings in FY21 and FY22 are the COVID-19 lockdown and rebound.</p>

  <h2 id="by-sector">Growth by sector</h2>
  <PeriodTable heading="Real GVA, % y/y" n={5} rows={[
    { id: "gva_real_growth", label: "Total GVA" },
    ...sectors.map((s) => ({ id: `gva_${s}_growth`, indent: true })),
  ]} />

  <h2 id="by-spending">Growth by spending component</h2>
  <PeriodTable heading="Constant prices, % y/y" n={5} rows={[
    { id: "gdp_real_level", how: "yoy", label: "GDP" },
    { id: "pfce_real_level", how: "yoy", indent: true },
    { id: "gfce_real_level", how: "yoy", indent: true },
    { id: "gfcf_real_level", how: "yoy", indent: true },
    { id: "exports_real_level", how: "yoy", indent: true },
    { id: "imports_real_level", how: "yoy", indent: true },
  ]} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Computed from MoSPI's quarterly levels on the 2022-23 base (site calculations), so they can differ from published growth rates by rounding. GDP also includes change in stocks, valuables and discrepancies, which are not shown.</p>

  <StackedBars title="Contributions to real GDP growth" subtitle="Percentage points of the year-on-year growth rate; dots show growth computed from the same quarterly levels"
    rows={contrib.rows} total={contrib.total} interval="3 months" source="MoSPI national accounts (base 2022-23); site calculations." />
  <p class="chart-sub">Contribution = change in the component over four quarters ÷ GDP four quarters earlier; imports subtract from GDP. "Other" is what the spending components do not explain: change in stocks, valuables and the statistical discrepancy. It was {num(other.pp, 1)} percentage points in {period(other.period, "Q")}, which is large: read growth by component with that in mind.</p>

  <h2 id="nominal-real">Nominal and real</h2>
  <LineChart title="Nominal and real GDP growth" subtitle="% change on a year earlier, as published; the gap is GDP deflator inflation"
    lines={[{ id: "gdp_nominal_growth", label: "Nominal" }, { id: "gdp_real_growth", label: "Real" }]} years={10} />

  <h2 id="forecasts">Forecasts and sentiment</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Professional forecasters: growth and inflation" subtitle="Median forecast for the current financial year at each survey round, %; the year forecast changes each April"
      lines={[{ id: "spf_gdp_cur_fy", label: "Real GDP growth" }, { id: "spf_cpi_cur_fy", label: "CPI inflation" }]} years={2} />
    <LineChart title="Consumer confidence" subtitle="RBI surveys, index (100 = neutral; above 100 = optimism)"
      lines={[{ id: "uccs_fei", label: "Urban, year ahead" }, { id: "rccs_fei", label: "Rural, year ahead" }, { id: "uccs_csi", label: "Urban, now" }, { id: "rccs_csi", label: "Rural, now" }]} years={2} />
  </div>
  <PeriodTable heading="Median forecast, %, survey of professional forecasters" n={4} rows={[
    { id: "spf_gdp_cur_fy", label: "Real GDP growth, this FY" }, { id: "spf_gdp_next_fy", label: "Real GDP growth, next FY" },
    { id: "spf_cpi_cur_fy", label: "CPI inflation, this FY" }, { id: "spf_core_cpi_cur_fy", label: "Core CPI inflation, this FY" },
    { id: "spf_fiscal_deficit_cur_fy", label: "Centre's fiscal deficit, % of GDP, this FY" },
  ]} />
  <p class="chart-sub">RBI's bi-monthly Survey of Professional Forecasters and Consumer Confidence Surveys, released with each MPC decision. They are respondents' views, not RBI's. Columns are the months the results were released; some older rounds are missing because their PDFs use a different layout.</p>

  <h2>Still to come on this page</h2>
  <p class="chart-sub">Annual estimates (advance, provisional, revised) and how they were revised, RBI's growth projections, and a detail page with sector tables. Checklist: docs/guidebook/05-pages/growth.md.</p>
</Base>
